# METAL GEAR RISING: REVENGEANCE (PlatinumGames' 2014 PC port: 32-bit, DirectX 9 through DXVK)
# summary: native 4K via the PC Fix, locked 60 fps (x87 fast path, VSync pacing, MSAA off), 16x filtering, DualSense as an Xbox pad
# 32-bit: Proton's normal 32-bit path reaches the GPU through the i386 NVIDIA libraries in FEX's RootFS (DXVK finds
# the GB10). Don't set PROTON_USE_WOW64=1: under FEX it cannot start the game ("Failed to create process", 731).
# 16x anisotropic filtering keeps textures sharp at grazing angles. The port picks the display's lowest refresh rate
# (the TV offers 23.98 and 29.97 Hz modes too), and its logic and boss scripting assume exactly 60 fps: DXVK reports
# and uses 60 Hz whatever the game asks for. Supersampling (d3d9.forceSampleRateShading = True) was the 1080p plan;
# at 4K it waits for a measurement.
# Frame pacing: the PC Fix's own 60 fps cap (FPSMode = 1 in its ini) fights VSync at the TV's 59.94 Hz and drops
# about 2.5 frames a second: 57.7 fps (lows 54.6) in the prologue's first fight. With the fix uncapped (FPSMode = 2)
# and DXVK's limiter at 60 the same fight holds 59.9 (lowest second 59.9; 2026-10-15). The cap also keeps the
# game's 60 fps logic at its speed should VSync ever be off.
DXVK_CONFIG=d3d9.samplerAnisotropy = 16; d3d9.forceRefreshRate = 60; d3d9.maxFrameRate = 60
# The game is CPU-bound in FEX: as a 32-bit Windows program it returns every float through the x87 FPU, whose
# 80-bit precision FEX emulates in software. 64-bit doubles instead: 59.6 fps against 23.8 in the same VR scene
# (4K, everything High, MSAA off; 2026-10-14). MSAA must stay off at 4K: x2 drops to 50 fps (lows 35), x8 to 22.
FEX_X87REDUCEDPRECISION=1
# Unlimiter (Nexus 850, raises the game's heap and file limits; Raiden Remaster Remake needs it) loads through
# Ultimate ASI Loader as dinput8.dll in the game folder: Proton must prefer that native DLL to its own.
WINEDLLOVERRIDES=dinput8=n,b
# vkBasalt (CAS sharpening, profiles/vkbasalt/235460.conf) waits for an i386 build: the installed layer is arm64,
# which only 64-bit games load (through FEX's Vulkan thunk).
# The game only understands XInput pads: without raw HID, Proton's SDL backend presents a DualSense as an Xbox pad,
# with rumble (as for Divinity: Original Sin 2).
PROTON_DISABLE_HIDRAW=0x054c/0x0ce6,0x054c/0x0df2
# Wine asks PipeWire for so little buffering that the HDMI output underruns under load: 90 ms gives 1024-sample cycles.
PULSE_LATENCY_MSEC=90
# Proton's Xalia (controller navigation for launchers) is not needed: the game has its own controller support.
PROTON_USE_XALIA=0
